  :progress/schema-note "cloud-itonami-lei universe-expansion progress tracker, per ADR-2607199960. Distinct from the sibling ISIC/ISCO classification-sampling progress files: this file's company source is real, published stock-index constituent lists (one row per index), not an ISIC/ISCO top-N judgment call. Each :index/constituents entry that reaches :company/status :done gets the SAME cloud-itonami-lei-<LEI> repo treatment (real GLEIF LEI, real ToS fetch, provenance, no fabrication) as the ISIC/ISCO fleet -- and before creating any new repo, the LEI must be checked against ALL already-registered LEIs (this file + both sibling files) to avoid duplicate repos for a company that's already covered via an ISIC/ISCO row or another index. This file is the resume point for the next /loop iteration on the universe track (kept separate from the ISIC/ISCO resume points so the two tracks can proceed independently without stepping on each other)."
  :progress/resume-from "Iteration 3 done 2026-07-19 (same session day, third /loop pass). sp500 is :index/status :in-progress with 22 constituents attempted total (11 :done, 11 :tos-fetch-failed) -- see that row's :index/constituents and :index/note. This iteration attempted 8 previously-untried candidates chosen for pharma/tech/consumer diversity: Salesforce, Inc. (done), Netflix, Inc. (done), Eli Lilly and Company (tos-fetch-failed), AbbVie Inc. (tos-fetch-failed), Meta Platforms, Inc. (tos-fetch-failed), Colgate-Palmolive Company (tos-fetch-failed), Kimberly-Clark Corporation (tos-fetch-failed), Mondelez International, Inc. (tos-fetch-failed). Only 2/8 succeeded this pass (lower than iterations 1-2) -- all 6 failures were genuine network-layer bot-blocks or client-rendered-SPA content unreachable via curl/WebFetch (Cloudflare challenge pages, GoDaddy parked-domain redirects revealing colgatepalmolive.com is not the real corporate domain, 400s on every Facebook/Meta legal URL guessed, and a heavy client-side-rendered Mondelez site where neither curl nor WebFetch could retrieve server-rendered legal body text, only nav-shell markup) -- see :index/note for full per-company detail. Companies NOT yet attempted for sp500 (real, well-known S&P 500 constituents): Citigroup Inc., Morgan Stanley, Berkshire Hathaway Inc., Chubb Limited, MetLife Inc., Honeywell International Inc., Deere & Company, Apple Inc., Alphabet Inc. -- resume by GLEIF-verifying and ToS-fetching more of these (dedup against the LEIs already in this row + both sibling progress files first) until sp500 reaches a documented stopping point, then mark :index/status :done and move to nikkei225 (next in file order), followed by topix100, ftse100, dax40, stoxx600, hangseng, csi300, asx200, tsx60, sensex, kospi200, bovespa, cac40, smi in that order. Same per-company discipline throughout: real GLEIF LEI only, real ToS fetch (curl with a standard browser User-Agent first, WebFetch as a second-method fallback for JS-shell/client-rendered pages -- note WebFetch tends to paraphrase/summarize rather than return true verbatim text even when explicitly instructed otherwise, so curl+plain-text-extraction remains the preferred method whenever the raw HTML actually contains server-rendered content), never fabricate, never substitute a subsidiary LEI for a parent, record failures honestly, dedup against this file + both sibling ISIC/ISCO progress files before creating any repo -- ALSO cross-check the live `gh api orgs/cloud-itonami/repos` listing since the pre-extracted registered-LEI snapshot can itself go stale between iterations. This superproject checkout has heavy concurrent multi-session activity -- always re-read this file fresh immediately before editing (this iteration again hit a shallow-clone false-positive 'forced update'/'unrelated histories' on fetch, confirmed via `gh api .../compare` to be a pure 8-commit fast-forward, resolved with `git fetch --deepen=30` rather than treating it as a real force-push), and prefer a worktree outside the superproject + feature branch + `gh api .../merges` server-side merge over direct edits in the shared checkout. Separately this iteration, isco-1341 (Independent Child Care Services Management Practice) was topped up from 1 to 4 companies in the sibling isco-progress.edn file -- see that file's :progress/resume-from for its own next-step detail; not duplicated here."
